\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 The Methodology Bridge Pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Educational essays within the Sources UI must not directly manipulate engine calculations. Instead, Helm employs a 
\f0\b Methodology Bridge Pattern
\f1\b0 . When an athlete reads an educational essay (e.g., "The Case for Stretch-Mediated Hypertrophy") and taps "Apply Methodology," the UI triggers an explicit configuration prompt. This action updates typed, deterministic settings (e.g., setting 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Exercise Selection Bias
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  to 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 STRETCH_FOCUSED
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ). The methodology text remains an educational citation, while the typed setting executes deterministic adjustments within the engine.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

