\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Per-Exercise Set Cap
\f1\b0 : No single exercise may receive more than 4 working sets in a single workout session. If a target muscle requires 6 hard sets in a workout, the engine 
\f0\b must
\f1\b0  split that volume across two distinct movement pattern slots (e.g., 3 sets of Vertical Pull + 3 sets of Horizontal Row).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Primary vs. Secondary Allocation Ratios
\f1\b0 : Mandatory primary compound slots are assigned 3 to 4 working sets. Secondary isolation slots are assigned 2 to 3 working sets.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Session Set Minimum Threshold
\f1\b0 : A standard 60-minute session must contain a minimum of 12 hard sets across at least 4 distinct exercises.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Criteria for 2-Exercise Sessions
\f1\b0 : A 2-exercise session is classified as an engine composition defect unless one of the following explicit parameters is present:\
